HIC Kernel
=========

HIC (Hierarchical Isolation Core) is a multi-architecture microkernel with a
three-tier privilege architecture, IPC 3.0 (entry-page self-check cross-domain
call), per-core capability slot partitioning, and formal specifications
(Isabelle/HOL).

Supported architectures:
- x86_64 (QEMU, UEFI)
- ARM64 (QEMU virt, GICv3, PL011)

Quick Start
-----------

ARM64 (QEMU):

  make ARCH=arm64
  make ARCH=arm64 run

x86_64 (UEFI):

  cd build && make

Build output goes to build/ for both architectures.

Architecture
------------

- Three-layer model: Core-0 (Ring 0), Privileged-1 (Ring 0, MMU isolated),
  Application-3 (Ring 3)
- IPC 3.0: call [entry_page] -> bt [bitmap] -> jmp [business_page]
- Per-core capability slot allocation (no global lock)
- TLV boot protocol (bootloader writes to 0x50000000, kernel reads)
- Static interrupt routing table (timer entry built at compile time)

